      "description": "Connect With Us | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Connect With Us Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Connect With Us Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Drop-In Hours - No Appointment Needed (Current Students) - Academic Year Only If you've never met with us before, we recommend that you start with a drop-in appointment, which are available from 11:00AM - 2:00 PM, Monday through Friday, no appointment necessary. Drop-in appointments are conducted by our Peer Career Advisors (PCA) , a highly trained team of student staff who can help you with a variety of topics. Not sure what you need? Come see us and we'll help you figure it out. Drop-in hours are not available during the summer.  If you need career support, please schedule an appointment with one of our Career Engagement Specialists. Booking An Appointment With A Professional Staff Member If you've met with a PCA or you are an alumnus , you can also meet with a professional staff member. You can book an appointment with us through the following links: Suzanne Brache : Student Employment Specialist Jonathan Chalmers : School of Business and School of Communications John Fracchia : School of Music, Theatre, & Dance Amy Huang : School of Humanities & Sciences Nico Lanari : School of Health Sciences & Human Performance The CCED Team Suzanne Brache Student Employment Specialist Jonathan Chalmers Career Engagement Specialist, School of Business Nico Lanari Career Engagement Specialist, School of Health Sciences and Human Performance Katrina Clark Associate Director, Experiential Learning and Employer Engagement Dave Curry Director John Fracchia Career Engagement and Technology Specialist, School of Health Sciences and Human Performance Amy Huang Career Engagement Specialist, School of Humanities and Sciences Meet Our Peer Career Advisors (PCAs) - highly trained student employees who are available for drop-ins in the Career Center Monday - Friday from 11am-2pm Angel Angel is a senior majoring in International Business and Advertising, Public Relations & Marketing Communications Colleen Colleen is a senior Advertising, Public Relations, and Marketing Comm major with minors in Graphic Design and Communication. Gaby Gaby is a junior Accounting major with a Business Analytics minor. Jacob Jacob is a junior Documentary Studies and Production major with minors in Marketing, Entrepreneurship & Innovation, and Psych. Jagrit Jagrit is a junior Computer Science major at Ithaca College. Juno Juno Brooks is a fourth year politics major with a history minor. Kamai Kamai is a sophomore Speech-Language Pathology major with an Education Studies minor. Leah Leah is sophomore Occupational Therapy major with a Communication Disorders minor. Nina Nina is a senior Health Sciences Major with a minor in Chemistry. Tamanna Tamanna is a junior Finance major with a minor in Entrepreneurship and Innovation. Ty Ty is a junior Environmental Science and Strategic Leadership double major, with an Entrepreneurship and Innovation minor. Sasha Sasha Culver is a graduate student studying Speech Language Pathology and Audiology. Contact Us Muller Faculty Center 101 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 Office Hours: M-F from 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM Drop-In Hours: M-F from 11:00 AM - 2:00 PM Meet Our Staff careers@ithaca.edu 607-274-3365 Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Polic