    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/who-we-support/first-year-student": {
      "title": "First Year Student",
      "description": "First Year Student | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search First Year Student Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Who We Support / First Year Student Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Here are some tips for making the most out of your First Year at Ithaca College. Learn How to Create Your Own Plan You DO NOT need to know what you want to do with the rest of your life when you start college.  Starting the conversation, however, can help you sort through alternatives and help you better map out possible options. Meet with CCED staff to learn how to get started and develop a personalized 4-year career plan . Assess What Matters to You Assess your personal values, interests, skills and abilities through career self-assessment tools such as the: Strong Interest Inventory (SII) - We recommend the Strong Interest Inventory to help students match their interests with potential careers, providing insights into fields that align with their passions and skills. Myers-Briggs Type Indicator (MBTI) - We recommend the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator to help students discover their personality type as it relates to their potential career goals. This tool offers insights into preferences, which can help guide academic and career choices. Email careers@ithaca.edu if you'd like to take either assessment. Research New Fields The best way to find out  about an occupation is through research and by meeting people in the field.  Alumni and industry professionals can help you learn more through informational interviews and job shadowing. Two excellent research sites to get you started are: O-Net The Occupational Outlook Handbook Immerse Yourself in Opportunities There are many ways to get involved on-campus and in the Ithaca community.  Here are three: Student organizations Volunteer On-campus job Find a Summer Experience Get a summer job that will provide you with an opportunity to learn about a career field that interests you.  Here are some resources to help: Handshake CareerShift Internships.com Try Your Hardest Do your best work academically.  It can be a transition adjusting to college level work and here are some resources to help you. Academic Support Tutoring Services Writing Center It's never to early to start taking advantage of all that CCED has to offer! Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/who-we-support/second-year-student": {
      "title": "Second Year Student",
      "description": "Second Year Student | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Second Year Student Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Who We Support / Second Year Student Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Second Year: Career Exploration & Leadership Development Here are some tips for making the most out of your Second Year at Ithaca College. Advice for Second Year students. Evaluate Your Plan Meet with a CCED staff member to discuss your career plans and evaluate your 4-year career plan. You still DO NOT need to know what you want to do with the rest of your life when you start college, but now is the time to start thinking about it.   Meet with CCED staff to learn how to get started and develop a personalized 4-year career plan . Explore Careers of Interest The best way to find out  about an occupation is through research and by meeting people in the field.  Two excellent research sites to get you started are: O-Net The Occupational Outlook Handbook Learn About the Career Selection Process Attend career related workshops to learn about the process of choosing a major or career path and attend programs featuring guest speakers from career fields that interest you. Learn with First-Hand Accounts Alumni and industry professionals can help you learn more through informational interviews and job shadowing. Conduct informational interviews with professionals to learn about a particular career field. LinkedIn is a great place to find Ithaca alumni in many fields! Develop Your Skills through Student Organizations Take an active role in a student organization to develop your communication, teamwork and problem-solving skills. Student organizations Refine Your Resume & Practice Your Interviewing Skills Develop a resume and have it critiqued by CCED. Also complete a mock interview to prepare for your summer job or internship search.  Our quick guides can help you get started in these areas: Resume Cover Letters Interviewing Secure Your Summer Opportunity Secure an internship or summer employment related to your career goals.  Here are some resources that can help you identify opportunities: Handshake CareerShift Internships.com Use your time at IC to connect with alumni and employers Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/who-we-support/third-year-student": {
      "title": "Third Year Student",
      "description": "Third Year Student | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Third Year Student Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Who We Support / Third Year Student Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Here are some tips for making the most out of your Third Year at Ithaca College. Tips for third year students. Create a Post-Grad Plan Meet with a CCED staff member to formulate your job or graduate school search timeline and plans. Establish Your Goals Focus and set career goals. At this time, all the experience and information you have gathered should be crystallizing into solid career goals and plans . Join a Chapter Join student chapters of professional organizations to gain career information and to start networking. Take Concrete Steps toward Grad School Research graduate/professional school possibilities , the application procedures and deadlines. Start Preparing for Your Admission Tests Register and prepare for admission tests such as the GRE , LSAT and MCAT or GMAT . Get to Know Potential Employers Participate in career fairs and career related events to explore your options and network with potential employers. Learn from Alumni's Experiences Get to know alumni and actively network with professionals in your area of interest. Step into a Leadership Role Take on leadership roles on and off-campus. Gain Experience over the Summer Get professional experience through on-campus research, an internship, on-campus employment, volunteer work or a summer job.  View opportunities in Handshake . CCED can help you with every step of your career journey Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
