ol Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Here are some tips for making the most out of your Fourth Year at Ithaca College. Tools To Build And Keep Momentum Refine Your Post-Grad Plan Meet with a Career Services staff member to design a job search strategy or finalize your graduate/professional school search timeline and plans. Hone Your Career-Related Skills at a Workshop Attend career related events targeted for seniors: Job and Internship Search, Resume Writing, Successful Interviewing, and more. Round Out Your Job Application Ask faculty and employers to be references for you. Learn More about Potential Employers Research companies/organizations and the career opportunities they offer.  Some good sites include: Handshake Glassdoor Schedule a Practice Run with Career Services Prepare for job interviews or graduate school with a mock interview in Career Services.  Our interview guide will help you get started. Start Your Job Search Engage in an active job search starting in the Fall semester. Attend Career Fairs and Events to Expand Your Network Participate in career fairs and other related events to build your network of contacts in your field of interest. Prepare Your Written Material Revise and update your resume and draft a cover letter . Complete Your Graduate School Applications For graduate school , complete your personal statement . Submit your applications to graduate schools.  Some helpful resources are: GradSchools.com Peterson’s Graduate School Guide Get More Experience! Complete an internship or career-related work experience if you haven’t already.  Some good resources are: Handshake Indeed.com CareerShift Apply for Employment Actively apply for positions. Attend networking events and make the connections for your job search. Prepare for a Change of Plans with an Alternate One Formulate an alternate “Plan B” in case you need to make last minute career adjustments. Career Services can help with job search and networking. We have alumni and employers eager to assist! Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/who-we-support/alumni": {
      "title": "Alumni",
      "description": "Alumni | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Alumni Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Who We Support / Alumni Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Welcome IC Alums! We strongly encourage alums to engage with CCED in a variety of ways! As an alumnus/a of Ithaca College, you have access to a variety of our services and resources during your career development process. Alumni may meet with a career counselor by appointment (via phone/ Zoom ).  Please contact our office at 607-274-3365 or by e-mail to schedule an appointment, or find the Career Engagement Specialist aligned with your school and click on their booking link .  You may also wish to view the Learn More About section of our website for in-depth information on most career topics. IC Alums – There are a number of virtual programs in which you are welcome to participate.  Scroll down to the bottom of this page to see them! Types Of Help Available: Below is a list of career topics for which alumni often seek out guidance: resume , cover letter and grad school essay development/reviews job search process graduate school application process interview practice networking strategies career goal clarification Online Resources : CCED maintains a powerful suite of tools that can be found under the Resources tab .  Our resources can be filtered by content/focus area. Help Us Build Learning And Career Development Opportunities CCED is always seeking out new opportunities, mentors, and partnerships as we help train the next generation of student leaders.  Please consider partnering with us to list opportunities, engage recruiters and speakers, blog, and build networks. In addition, if you would like to learn more or discuss more, please feel free to e-mail us at: careers@ithaca.edu . Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
