    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/equity-inclusion-and-belonging": {
      "title": "Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging",
      "description": "Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion At the Ithaca College Career Center, we are dedicated to fostering a welcoming, equitable, and inclusive environment. We are deeply committed to assisting our students and alumni throughout their life and career journeys, empowering them to advocate for human and civil rights both personally and professionally. As a cohesive team, we are relentless in our pursuit of continuous learning and professional growth, particularly in matters concerning equity, inclusion, and belonging for all students. Our Commitment Read more about our commitment to you here. Read More View our collection of resources by clicking the buttons below, or by navigating through the tabs on the left toolbar. Resources Explore resources geared towards BIPOC students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards first-generation students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards international students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards LGBTQIA+ students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards students and alumni who are neurodivergent or have a disability as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards students and alumni who are undocumented or have DACA status as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards veteran students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards women students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/equity-inclusion-and-belonging/equity-inclusion-and-belonging-our-commitment": {
      "title": "Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment",
      "description": "Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Our Commitment To Building A Welcoming, Equitable, & Inclusive Community The Center for Career Exploration and Development (CCED) affirms the Ithaca College Diversity Statement and commits to building and contributing to a campus community that is welcoming, equitable, and inclusive to individuals of all identities.  We affirm the need to recognize, analyze, and stand against systems of inequality. Our responsibility as educators is to inspire students to explore and uphold their values, find meaning in them, and encourage forward momentum. We acknowledge that it is also our responsibility as individuals to do this work. We commit to continuously: Recognize that career development is unique for every person, especially those who have been impacted by systemic disadvantages, marginalization, and exclusion Create a safe space where students can talk freely and openly, without judgement, about their identities and circumstances Increase student access to opportunities and resources, which includes educating employers on existing systems and practices that are exclusionary Seek out and develop relationships with employers who specifically value diversity and inclusion Ensure diverse representation in our programs and events to reflect our community’s intersecting experiences, identities, and abilities Ensure all efforts are made to recruit and hire diverse professional and student staff Actively and directly hear feedback via this online form from our community, then doing the work necessary to incorporate that feedback within the capacity of our resources It is our intent with this statement to create and refine tangible processes for measuring our progress. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
