      "title": "BIPOC Resources",
      "description": "BIPOC Resources | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search BIPOC Resources Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging / BIPOC Resources Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x BIPOC Resources While no two individual experiences are the same, this page shares some resources geared towards BIPOC students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Remember that Career Center staff is always available to meet to provide more individualized support and resources, or to connect you with alumni who have relatable identities or experiences. Note:  These resources all link to external sites. We are not responsible for any third-party site content and urge discretion when utilizing these resources. As part of our ongoing DEI commitment to our IC students and alumni, we share the below career resources.  If you have any questions, concerns, or suggestions about/for this page, feel free to email them to us at careers@ithaca.edu . Expand All General BIPOC Resources Diversity Employers​ Find jobs with employers committed to diversity. Diversity Jobs​ Connect with employers who seek diversity. Getting Hired​ Join CareerCircle, committed to inclusivity and expanding opportunities for diverse talents, including job seekers with disabilities. Insight Into Diversity​ Read the oldest and largest diversity magazine in higher education. Jopwell Explore Jopwell, a platform that represents and advances careers for Black, Latinx, and Native American students and professionals. National Urban League Jobs Network​ The National Urban League is a historic civil rights organization dedicated to economic empowerment in order to elevate the standard of living in historically underserved urban communities. Asian and Pacific Islander Ascend – Pan-Asian Leaders Join the platform that offers career lifecycle and cross-industry networking and mentorship opportunities, development and leadership opportunities. Asian Career Network Discover career opportunities, resources, events, and tools tailored for career growth within the Asian community. Conference on Asian Pacific American Leadership (CAPAL) Explore scholarship, internship, leadership, and professional development programs for the youth. Federal Asian Pacific American Council This is a nonprofit, nonpartisan organization that represents the civilian and military Asian Pacific American (APA) employees in the Federal and District of Columbia governments. National Association of Asian American Professionals (NAAAP), New York The National Association of Asian American Professionals – New York Chapter is a non-profit organization that cultivates and empowers Asian & Pacific Islander leaders through professional development, community service, and networking. National Council of Asian Pacific Americans (NCAPA) NCAPA represents the interests of the greater Asian American and Native Hawaiian Pacific Islander communities and provides a national voice for AA and NHPI issues. Black and African American Black Career Women’s Network (BCWN) Join the network and leverage the synergy of professional growth, strategic career planning, and workplace mastery. BlackJobs.com Utilize the website that features the latest well-paying job opportunities for African American job seekers from companies who are sincerely dedicated to diversity hiring. The Black EOE Journal Receive updates on the latest news, trends, and resources concerning diversity and inclusion in the workplace. United Negro College Fund (UNCF) Explore scholarships, internships, and resources at UNCF to support and empower African American students in their pursuit of higher education and career success. Indigenous and American Indian National Congress of American Indians (NCAI) Explore NCAI's website for vital resources on Native American advocacy, policy updates, and cultural preservation efforts. NativeAmericanJobs.com Visit Native American Jobs to explore career opportunities, connect with inclusive employers, and access resources tailored for Native American job seekers. Native America Today (NAT) Learn more about current news and explore thought-provoking journalism, that brings people closer together by broadening perspectives of Native peoples, marginalized by traditional stereotypical images. Native Hire Explore Native Hire to access job listings, career resources, and training opportunities designed to empower Native American job seekers. Ticket to Success: A College Guide for Indigenous Students Discover Snappy Words’ 'Ticket to Success' for guidance on college readiness, resources, and support tailored specifically for Indigenous students. Hispanic and Latinx Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute (CHCI) Explore opportunities for leadership development programs, internships, and fellowships that CHCI offers as part of their commitment to advancing Latinx representation in leadership across the United States. Hispanic Alliance for Career Engagement Engage with HACE to access career advancement programs, networking events, and resources fostering leadership and economic growth within the Hispanic community. Hispanic Association of Colleges & Universities (HACU) Access HACU's Student Programs for opportunities like scholarships, internships, and leadership development aimed at empowering students at Hispanic-Serving Institutions. iHispano Connect with employers who value diversity and inclusion, and unlock new career opportunities tailored for Hispanic professionals. LATCareers.com Explore LATCareers.com to discover career opportunities, resources, and events tailored to connect bilingual and Latino professionals with inclusive employers. Saludos Connect with opportunities on Saludos.com, a premier platform for bilingual Hispanic professionals seeking diverse careers and employers committed to inclusivity. Society for Advancement of Chicanos/Hispanics and Native Americans in Science (SACNAS) Refer to SACNAS for resources, community support, and opportunities in STEM tailored to empower Hispanics, and Native Americans. UnidosUS Explore UnidosUS to discover resources, advocacy initiatives, and programs that empower the Latino community in areas such as education, healthcare, and economic opportunities. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/equity-inclusion-and-belonging/first-generation-resources": {
      "title": "First-Generation Resources",
      "description": "First-Generation Resources | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search First-Generation Resources Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging / First-Generation Resources Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x First-Generation Resources While no two individual experiences are the same, this page shares some resources geared towards first-generation students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Remember that Career Center staff is always available to meet to provide more individualized support and resources, or to connect you with alumni who have relatable identities or experiences. Note:  These resources all link to external sites. We are not responsible for any third-party site content and urge discretion when utilizing these resources. As part of our ongoing DEI commitment to our IC students and alumni, we share the below career resources.  If you have any questions, concerns, or suggestions about/for this page, feel free to email them to us at careers@ithaca.edu . A Career Road Map for First-Generation Professionals Gain valuable insights and practical steps to navigate your professional journey as a first-generation professional with this comprehensive career roadmap. America Needs You Access transformative fellowship programs designed to empower first-generation college students with mentorship, career development, and tools for professional success. Beyond 12​ Get personolized coaching, utilize the app taiolored toward goal set up and completion, and use AI tools for strategic approach towards career building. Center for First Gen Student Success​ Consult for better understand the first-generation student experience, identify support strategies, and explore why advancing first-generation student success is a desirable outcome. FirstGen Fellows Engage with the Lawyers’ Committee’s FirstGEN Fellows Program to gain invaluable experience, mentorship, and training as a first-generation law student pursuing a career in civil rights advocacy. Project Basta Unlock career opportunities through Basta's free Fellowship, offering an 11-week career readiness intensive and ongoing career coaching. Resources for First-Generation College Students from EduMed Discover the resources and support you need as a first-generation college student in healthcare, find financial aid, and solutions to common challenges. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
