    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/equity-inclusion-and-belonging/lgbtqia-resources": {
      "title": "LGBTQIA+ Resources",
      "description": "LGBTQIA+ Resources | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search LGBTQIA+ Resources Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging / LGBTQIA+ Resources Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x LGBTQIA+ Resources While no two individual experiences are the same, this page shares some resources geared towards LGBTQIA+ students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Remember that Career Center staff is always available to meet to provide more individualized support and resources, or to connect you with alumni who have relatable identities or experiences. Note:  These resources all link to external sites. We are not responsible for any third-party site content and urge discretion when utilizing these resources. As part of our ongoing DEI commitment to our IC students and alumni, we share the below career resources.  If you have any questions, concerns, or suggestions about/for this page, feel free to email them to us at careers@ithaca.edu . 4 Job Search Tips for Transgender and Non-Binary People This article offers four job-search strategies tailored to help transgender and non-binary individuals navigate employment challenges and assert their identities in the hiring process. 5 Ways to Convey Your Pronoun of Choice At a New Job Engage with a community platform offering job opportunities, cash connects, reviews, and events, along with resources on sharing pronouns with new employers. Beyond the Binary: Navigating the Workplace as a Non-Binary Individual Explore how this platform supports work-life balance and employee well-being while offering job search tools and insights to help you find fulfilling career opportunities. Coming Out at Work Access tools and resources designed to support LGBTQ+ individuals, offering guidance for navigating the workplace, understanding legal rights, and fostering inclusive communities. Everywhere is Queer Explore resources, stories, and tools on this platform that empower LGBTQ+ individuals, featuring their app for mental health support, social justice advocacy, and fostering inclusivity in all aspects of life. Human Rights Campaign – Corporate Equality Index​ Explore the Corporate Equality Index to learn about how U.S. companies are ranked based on their policies and practices related to LGBTQ+ workplace equality. Lambda Legal Lambda Legal is a nonprofit civil rights organization that provides legal advocacy, representation, and education to defend the rights of LGBTQ+ people and those living with HIV. National Center for Transgender Equality Explore policy advocacy, public education, and resources such as ID document guidance, healthcare access support, and workplace protections National LGBT Chamber of Commerce The National LGBT Chamber of Commerce (NGLCC), the business voice of the LGBTQ community, is the only national advocacy organization dedicated to expanding economic opportunities for the LGBTQ business community. Out & Equal Learn about leadership development programs, on demand learning, southern states initiative, global impact programs, and more! Out Professionals Explore resources and networking opportunities tailored for LGBTQ+ professionals, including events, career tools, and membership options to foster connections and advance your career. Rainbow Center Access resources, advocacy, and safe spaces for the LGBTQIA+ community through the Rainbow Center. Transgender Employment Program Gain access to tailored job training, career fairs, mentorship, and supportive employer connections. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/equity-inclusion-and-belonging/neurodivergent-and-disability-resources": {
      "title": "Neurodivergent and Disability Resources",
      "description": "Neurodivergent and Disability Resources | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging / Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Neurodivergent and Disability Resources While no two individual experiences are the same, this page shares some resources geared towards students and alumni who are neurodivergent or have a disability as they navigate their career development. Remember that Career Center staff is always available to meet to provide more individualized support and resources, or to connect you with alumni who have relatable identities or experiences. Note:  These resources all link to external sites. We are not responsible for any third-party site content and urge discretion when utilizing these resources. As part of our ongoing DEI commitment to our IC students and alumni, we share the below career resources.  If you have any questions, concerns, or suggestions about/for this page, feel free to email them to us at careers@ithaca.edu . Chronically Capable This website focuses on empowering individuals with disabilities by offering resources, support, and opportunities for personal growth and community involvement. Department of Labor - Workforce Recruitment Program The Washington, D.C. Internship Program (WRP) connects college students with disabilities to paid summer internships in the federal government, providing career development opportunities and professional experience. Disability: IN - Disability Equality Index Compare companies' disability inclusion efforts using this comprehensive benchmarking tool. Job Accommodation Network JAN provides free, expert guidance on workplace accommodations and disability employment issues, helping employers and individuals create inclusive, accessible work environments. Lime Connect This platform connects students and professionals with disabilities to career opportunities, resources, and mentorship, promoting inclusion and accessibility in the workforce. Mentra: Neurodiversity Employment Network This website connects neurodivergent job seekers with inclusive employers, creating personalized career opportunities and promoting workplace diversity and acceptance. Neurodiversity Employment Network ​ Browse job opportunities, resources, video testimonials and newsletters from this group that is committed to advancing employment opportunities for neurodivergent individuals. Neurodiversity in Business This platform is dedicated to connecting neurodivergent individuals with inclusive employment opportunities, focusing on matching talents with supportive employers. Neurodiversity Network This global community advocates for neurodivergent individuals, provides resources, support, and connections to foster inclusive workplaces and societal change. Programs Programs.com offers a comprehensive resources regarding cybersecurity education and careers for people with disabilities. Resume and Employment Guide for People with Disabilities Check out this resume and career advice tailored specifically for people with disabilities to help navigate the job market with confidence and accessibility. Viscardi Center Find job seekers, employers, educators, and service providers working to enable neurodivergent individuals to gain meaningful employment. Washington DOIT Look through this platform to find technology, resources, and support to help students with disabilities succeed in education, careers, and life. Workforce Recruitment Program Connect with federal and private sector employees offering valuable internships and career opportunities while promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/equity-inclusion-and-belonging/undocumented-and-daca-resources": {
      "title": "Undocumented and DACA Resources",
