eating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Undocumented and DACA Resources While no two individual experiences are the same, this page shares some resources geared towards students and alumni who are undocumented or have DACA status as they navigate their career development. Remember that Career Center staff is always available to meet to provide more individualized support and resources, or to connect you with alumni who have relatable identities or experiences. Note:  These resources all link to external sites. We are not responsible for any third-party site content and urge discretion when utilizing these resources. As part of our ongoing DEI commitment to our IC students and alumni, we share the below career resources.  If you have any questions, concerns, or suggestions about/for this page, feel free to email them to us at careers@ithaca.edu . About DACA and Employment ​ Read about essential information and resources about DACA and employment rights, empowering recipients to navigate the workforce confidently. DREAMer Jobs This Facebook group posts job openings for DACA beneficiaries and offers a space for them to reach out and network with others. Immigrants Rising: Life After College This resource empowers undocumented students with tools and guidance to navigate post-college challenges, from job searching to legal support. Immigrants Rising Resources Browse these resources that offer support for undocumented immigrants navigating education, employment, and legal pathways. My Undocumented Life This platform shares stories, resources, and support for undocumented immigrants, fostering community and advocacy for their rights and experiences. Northwest Immigrant Rights Project This site offers legal assistance and advocacy for immigrants, ensuring access to justice and protecting their rights through the Pacific Northwest. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
