      "title": "Faculty Toolkit",
      "description": "Faculty Toolkit | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Faculty Toolkit Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Faculty Toolkit Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Faculty Toolkit﻿ ﻿CCED is happy to help you infuse career content and articulate professional relevance into your programming however it fits you. Let's discuss your ideas or, we can create new ones together! The Center for Career Exploration and Development Wants to Help You Help Your Students While career guidance is not a requirement at Ithaca College, it is an increasing priority for students and prospective students and their supporters. We are here to help you add resources and support options to keep you and your students updated on our workforce, and what they need to do now to prepare for it. How Can We Help You? Have us in to speak to your class about virtually any topic related to careers. Advise students to meet with us as a part of your programming. Promote career events, fairs, workshops and other opportunities that we offer in your presentations. Incorporate National Association for Colleges and Employers (NACE) career competencies into your syllabus to show students how your course helps prepare them for their career. (see p. 3). CAREER CENTER KEY FOCUS AREAS Creating a Personalized Career Plan Interest and Personality Assessments Grad School Planning Self-Promotion and Branding Application Material Review Job and internship Searching Alumni and Employer Networking CAREER CENTER RESOURCES Daily Drop-In Hours School-Specific Career Engagement Specialists Career Quest - A Personalized Career Journey Big Interview - AI Interview Prep Free to IC Access to an Interview Room Free Professional Head Shot Photo Booth Career Closet to Borrow Professional Attire Student Employment Jobs and Support Internship Financial Assistance Free LinkedIn Learning Trainings EVENTS AND OPPORTUNITIES Employer Recruitment Visits Guest Speakers Job Shadow Trips Career Fairs Career-Related Workshops and Trainings INFORMATIONAL SLIDES TO ADD TO POWERPOINTS In-Person Resources Online Resources Handshake Job Search Platform How to Book Head Shot Photo Booth Student Employment Jobs and Support Internship Financial Assistance Career Center Instagram Page Career Corner Podcast CCED Staff TOP 8 CAREER COMPETENCIES THAT TODAY’S EMPLOYERS WANT... AND THAT YOUR COURSE MAY PROVIDE! Communication Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with persons inside and outside of an organization. Critical Thinking Identify and respond to needs based upon an understanding of situational context and logical analysis of relevant information. Professionalism Knowing work environments differ greatly, understand and demonstrate effective work habits, and act in the interest of the larger community and workplace. Equity and Inclusion Demonstrate the awareness, attitude, knowledge, and skills required to equitably engage and include people from different cultures and backgrounds. Leadership Recognize and capitalize on personal and team strengths to achieve organizational goals. Teamwork Build and maintain collaborative relationships to work effectively toward common goals, while appreciating diverse viewpoints and shared responsibilities. Career & Self-Development Proactively develop oneself and one’s career through continual personal and professional learning, awareness of one’s strengths and weaknesses, navigation of career opportunities, and networking. Technology Understand and leverage technologies ethically to enhance efficiencies, complete tasks, and accomplish goals. * These competencies can be highlighted in your syllabus or assignments to articulate how your course is helping to prepare students for their career, regardless of what that may be. Source: National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) How Can Faculty Connect With Us? REQUEST FORM Whether it is to seek guidance on how to infuse career competencies into your syllabus or assignments, to discuss a collaboration opportunity, or simply to learn more about infusing career-related content into your courses, please fill out a request form here . SCHOOL-BASED SPECIALISTS You can connect directly with the Career Engagement Specialist assigned to your school. You can find them in the graphic below, and they can be contacted at this link . HIRING TA’S And because the Career Center is also the new home of Student Employment, you can reach out for guidance on hiring a TA. More info on that can be found here . Please feel free to email us at Careers@ithaca.edu with any questions. We look forward to helping you help your students! Want this information in PDF format? Download our guide with clickable links here . Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
