and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Build Meaningful Connections with Ithaca College Students Whether you're looking to hire students or recent graduates, host interns, share industry expertise, or build connections with the Ithaca College community, we're here to help. We welcome partnerships that support student success while helping organizations meet their talent and engagement goals. Schedule an Employer Consultation Not sure where to start? Meet with Katrina Clark, the Associate Director of Experiential Learning & Employer Engagement to discuss your organization's goals and explore ways to connect with Ithaca College students. Whether you're interested in hiring recent graduates, participating in on-campus events, developing early talent, or broader partnership opportunities, we're happy to help identify the best fit! Click the \"Schedule Here\" button below or email Katrina at kclark3@ithaca.edu to set up a consultation meeting. Schedule Here Why Partner with Ithaca College? \"Theory, Practice, Performance\" is Ithaca College's motto and reflects our commitment to connecting classroom learning with real-world application. Our students bring strong academic preparation, hands-on experience, and a wide range of perspectives to internships, projects, employment opportunities, and community partnerships. More than 70 majors and nearly 70 minors across 5 schools Experiential learning opportunities including internships, research, clinical placements, creative work, and community engagement Career-ready students with strengths in communication, critical thinking, teamwork, leadership, and professionalism Strong alumni network spanning industries Students from diverse academic backgrounds including business, communications, health sciences, humanities, sciences, music, theatre, and dance Recruit Through Handshake Handshake is Ithaca College's primary recruiting platform and the best way to share jobs, internships, events, and other opportunities with students and alumni. Handshake is used by colleges and universities across the nation. By creating an account, employers can share opportunities not only with Ithaca College students but, once approved, expand visibility to additional institutions across the Handshake network. Through Handshake, employers can: Post jobs and internships Promote events and information sessions Register for career fairs Build awareness of your organization Connect with students and early talent Check out Handshake's How to Create an Employer Account article & sign up using the Join Handshake button below. We also encourage you to explore Handshake's Employer Academy with a variety of on-demand training courses and quick tip videos tailored to employers. If you're new to Handshake, there are courses on how to get started and learn the basics. For further support, check out the Handshake Help Center and/or connect with Katrina Clark, Ithaca College's Associate Director of Experiential Learning & Employer Relations at kclark3@ithaca.edu . Join Handshake Engagement Opportunities There are many ways to engage with Ithaca College students and alumni. We welcome conversations about how to tailor partnership opportunities to meet your organization's goals. Recruiting Post jobs and internships Attend career fairs Host information sessions Conduct on-campus interviews Participate in auditions, portfolio reviews, and/or talent showcases Join us for networking events Industry Engagement & Student Learning Host an Employer Lunch & Learn Participate in career treks and site visits Serve as a guest speaker or panelist Partner on project-based learning experiences Offer informational interviews Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
