    "https://twitter.com/iccareers": {
      "title": "IC Center for Career Exploration & Development",
      "description": "IC Center for Career Exploration & Development (@iccareers) / X Log in Sign up IC Center for Career Exploration & Development 6,632 posts IC Center for Career Exploration & Development @iccareers Our lifetime service is dedicated to helping Ithaca College students and alumni through all stages of their career journeys! Ithaca College, Ithaca, NY linktr.ee/ICCareerCenter Joined August 2009 286 Following 1,424 Followers Mention Follow Posts Posts Replies Replies Reposts Reposts Media Media Log in or sign up for X See what’s happening and join the conversation Continue with phone Continue with Apple Continue with Google or Log in with username or email Terms · Privacy · Cookies · Accessibility · US TIDA · Ads Info · More © 2026 X Corp. IC Center for Career Exploration & Development @iccareers Oct 31, 2025 If you're planning to be in Ithaca over November break, consider volunteering at the Food Bank of the Southern Tier! You must RSVP on Engage to participate. 1 54 IC Center for Career Exploration & Development @iccareers May 8, 2025 A heartfelt appreciation to our producer, Kylie Schultz, and our host, Lukas Kauffman, for their incredible contributions to the #CareerCornerPodcast 🎙️ 42 IC Center for Career Exploration & Development @iccareers May 7, 2025 Season Four of the #CareerCornerPodcast 🎙️is streaming on YouTube and Spotify. Dive into inspiring stories and guidance from IC alumni, students, and faculty. Be sure not to miss it, and we look forward to seeing you next season! 15 IC Center for Career Exploration & Development @iccareers May 2, 2025 Tune into the final episode of the #CareerCornerPodcast 🎙️ featuring Mish Lenhart, the Director of Student Engagement, as she shares insights on Professional Involvement and Leadership! 12 IC Center for Career Exploration & Development @iccareers Apr 25, 2025 Explore February's role as a Community Coordinator at the LGBTQ Center on the #CareerCornerPodcast 🎙️ Discover the center's resources, community events, and dive into the significance of queer visibility in media! 5"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/career-corner-podcast": {
      "title": "Career Corner Podcast",
      "description": "Career Corner Podcast | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Career Corner Podcast Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Career Corner Podcast Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Welcome To The Career Corner! Come on in! Our weekly podcast will give you career and life resources, cool tips, and insights from alumni and staff. Subscribe for latest news and episodes Episode 05: In this episode, Lukas interviews IC alums and small business owners, Lee and Lauren, who operate Gardella's Goodies in the Ithaca community. Episode 04:  In this episode, Lukas explores the Audio Production & The Storytelling Realm with IC Alum, Vedant Akhauri. Newest Episodes: Season Four is Here! Episode 03: In This episode, Lukas interviews IC alum Lisa Famularo, a career development specialist at the University of Connecticut (UCONN) and former Peer Career Advisor at IC. Episode 02:  In This episode, Lukas interviews Mullen Quaye, A Medical Assistant and Tompkins County Human Rights Commission Volunteer, on Public Health Careers. In episode 1, Lukas explores relationship & self-care tips with mental health therapist, Arielle Manganiello. Season Three Episodes Episode 9: Meet Maddy Blomkvist a sports management alum who works on data analytics for the NFL. Episode 8: Lukas interviews IC alum Hana Matoki, a pediatric occupational therapist. Episode 7: Lukas interviews Jason Starkman and Sam Edelstein about their experience in tech startups and politics with their app, Poliquicks. Episode 6: Meet Muhammed Cisse and IC alum and current graduate student studying social work. Episode 5: IC faculty member, Ian Woods and Sam Elebiary, the Career Center's Associate Director for Career Engagement & Education talk about their Peace Corps experience. Episode 4: IC students Matt Minton and Sena Numkung talk with Lukas about their student internship experiences. Episode 3: Lukas interviews IC alum and Mental Health Professional, Jennifer Ochiaga, on maintaining positive mental health while in college. Episode 2: The career center's Student Employment Specialist, Hope Borsic, spills the tea on the world of student employment. Episode 1: Season 3 kicks off with the Susan DiPace Alumni Panel. SEASON TWO EPISODES EPISODE 11:  In this episode we hear about the value of volunteering with non-profit organizations. Episode 11: Volunteering for Non-Profit Organizations Audio file In this episode we explore the ins and outs of studying in London. Episode 10: In this episode we explore the ins and outs of studying in London. Episode 10: Studying In London - What You Need To Know Audio file Episode 09:  In this episode Lukas delves into the tools and resources for finding scholarships. Episode 09: Navigating Scholarship Opportunities Audio file Episode 08:  In Episode 8 Lukas discusses the student-athlete experience with IC athletes Anya Watkins (basketball) and Ashan Chandrasena (rowing). Episode 8: The Student-Athlete Experience Audio file episode 07: In episode 7 we explore whether joining clubs are beneficial post-grad. Episode 7: Are The Clubs I Join Now Beneficial Post-Grad? Audio file Episode 06: In episode 6 Lukas asks the question, \"Can you succeed with a double major?\" Episode 6: Can I Successfully Double Major? Audio file Episode 05:  In episode 5, Lukas peers behind the scenes of TV News. Episode 5: Behind The Scenes Of TV News Audio file Episode 04:  Scott Lozea- Director of Post Production at NBC Sports, discusses what it's like to work in post-production. Episode 04: Post Production In Sports Media Audio file Episode 03: In this episode, we discuss finding confidence in career readiness. Episode 3: Finding Confidence In Career Readiness Audio file Episode 02: In this episode, we explore confidence, competence and following your dreams. Episode 2:  Confidence and Competence: Following Your Dreams Audio file Episode 01: In the first episode of Season 2, Lukas interviews alumna Alexa Chalnik on songwriting, content creation, and networking. Episode 1 Audio file Season One Episodes Episode 1: Succeeding In College Audio file In our inaugural episode, Career Engagement Specialists Brielle Long (Humanities & Sciences) & Cooper Rothman (School of Music, Theatre, & Dance) talk about their roles and how the Center for Career Exploration & Development helps Ithaca College students and alumni. Episode 2: Starting Your Own Media Brand Audio file In episode 2, host Lukas Kauffman interviews IC alums Eden Strachan , a journalist and social justice filmmaker, and Christina Chironna , co-founder of FilmUp. Episode 3: Social Justice & Entrepreneurship Audio file In episode 3, Lukas interviews IC alums Rita Bunatal and Via Carpenter who discuss their journey as entrepreneurs with a social justice mindset. Episode 4: Is Grad School for Me? Audio file In episode 4, Lukas interviews faculty members Peter Martin (Education) and Margaret Shackell (Business) who discuss the pros and cons of graduate education. Episode 5: Exploring Careers In Education Audio file In episode 5, Lukas interviews Education Department faculty members Sara Levy (Education) and Shuzhan Li who discuss careers in education and share their own journeys. Episode 6: Creative Careers in Writing Audio file In episode 6, Lukas interviews writers Steven Salvatore and Meg Marzella who discuss creative careers in writing. Episode 7: How To Nail Job Interviews Audio file In episode 7, Lukas interviews Career Engagement Specialists Suzanne Brache (Park) and Jonathan Chalmers (Business) who discuss how to nail job (and internship) interviews. Episode 8: Careers In Environmental Science Audio file In episode 8, Lukas interviews Mary McKean (Project Specialist, National Park Service) and Julia DiGeronimo (Environmental Educator and Bee Keeper) about careers in the environmental science space. Episode 9: Advice from a Physical Therapist and Entrepreneur Audio file In episode 9, Lukas interviews Bryan Guzski, a physical therapist and entrepreneur. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/inspiring-internships/mckenna-brennan-28": {
      "title": "Inspiring Internships",
      "description": "McKenna Brennan '28 | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Inspiring Internships Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Inspiring Internships / McKenna Brennan '28 Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x McKenna Brennan '28 By   Roy H. Park School of Communications, May 7, 2026 Creative Intern, American High Social Media Intern, Purple Banana “If I didn't receive hands-on experience from the first day, I wouldn't have been prepared for two internships coming out of my freshman year.” A Semester in Production McKenna Brennan ‘28 felt drawn to IC's Park School for its resources and its emphasis on experience from day one. She didn’t hesitate to embrace roles on campus as a Producer for the Career Corner podcast and Social Media Director of Park Promotions. In fact, those positions helped earn McKenna a Creative Internship at American High, a local production group, and a Social Media Internship at Purple Banana, an acai cafe. \"I was set up right away to take on a leadership role,” says McKenna. Working on the Career Corner Podcast connected McKenna with dozens of alumni, faculty, staff, and students as she coordinated interviews and recordings. She also learned how to edit and upload footage to various platforms, promoting the podcast on social media. The experience equipped McKenna with the concrete skills and confidence she needed to apply to content creation and account management during her internships.“All of my professors and extracurriculars have paved the way for my professional growth.” McKenna had already built a connection with American High during high school, but it was her work on the Career Corner Podcast that helped her become a qualified strategic communicator ready to tackle assignments for the production company with over four million subscribers. In the role, McKenna managed three social media accounts and led promotions for American High’s New York State High School Film Festival. “I discovered that I love to be able to reflect on my past and offer opportunities to support the creative community.” Her work helped publicize the accomplishments of high school students and aspiring filmmakers, a position she was once in. “I also found the joy in being able to work for myself and come up with ideas for content that other people find inspiring.” McKenna has harnessed social media as a tool for building community and amplifying the stories she values. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/inspiring-internships/colleen-golden-27": {
      "title": "Inspiring Internships",
      "description": "Colleen Golden '27 | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Inspiring Internships Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Inspiring Internships / Colleen Golden '27 Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Colleen Golden '27 By   Roy H. Park School of Communications, February 2, 2026 Public Relations Intern, Hollywood Agency Graphic Design Intern, Arocam Sports A Summer in Strategic Communications An Advertising, Public Relations and Marketing Communications major with minors in Graphic Design and Communication Strategy Design, Colleen Golden ‘27 spent her summer balancing two internships. She states, “this allowed me to explore multiple areas within my field of study and define my career goals.” Half of Colleen’s week was spent as a Graphic Design Intern at Arocam Sports, where she designed branding for teams and created promotional materials used in stadium installations and website inserts. The other half was spent at Hollywood Agency as a Public Relations Intern, where she was responsible for compiling media lists, as well as creating social media posts and industry reports for clients. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/center-career-exploration-and-development/inspiring-internships/abygail-sevegny-26": {
      "title": "Inspiring Internships",
      "description": "Abygail Sevegny '26 | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Inspiring Internships Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Inspiring Internships / Abygail Sevegny '26 Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Abygail Sevegny '26 By   Roy H. Park School of Communications, January 30, 2026 Merchandising Intern TJX Companies A Summer in Corporate Retail Abygail Sevegny ‘26, an Advertising, Public Relations and Marketing Communications major with a Media Literacy minor, has had her sights set on corporate retail since as far back as she can remember. When she was offered the chance to return to the TJX Companies for the second summer as a Merchandising Intern, she knew she had to take advantage of the opportunity. Her role combines her analytical skills with trend tracking, and sets her up for continuing success in her field. At the conclusion of her internship, Abby was offered a full-time offer at the TJX Companies following her graduation! Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/career-services/diversity-equity-inclusion": {
      "title": "Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging",
      "description": "Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion At the Ithaca College Career Center, we are dedicated to fostering a welcoming, equitable, and inclusive environment. We are deeply committed to assisting our students and alumni throughout their life and career journeys, empowering them to advocate for human and civil rights both personally and professionally. As a cohesive team, we are relentless in our pursuit of continuous learning and professional growth, particularly in matters concerning equity, inclusion, and belonging for all students. Our Commitment Read more about our commitment to you here. Read More View our collection of resources by clicking the buttons below, or by navigating through the tabs on the left toolbar. Resources Explore resources geared towards BIPOC students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards first-generation students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards international students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards LGBTQIA+ students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards students and alumni who are neurodivergent or have a disability as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards students and alumni who are undocumented or have DACA status as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards veteran students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Resources Explore resources geared towards women students and alumni as they navigate their career development. Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.ithaca.edu/career-services/about": {
      "title": "Connect With Us",
      "description": "Connect With Us | Ithaca College Skip to main content Athletics Alumni Events News Apps Connect Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. myIC Canvas Engage GIVE VISIT Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Campus Map Directions Virtual Tour APPLY Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Graduate Academics Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Our Schools Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Business Communications Health Sciences and Human Performance Humanities and Sciences Music, Theatre, and Dance Academic Calendar & Registrar Graduate and Professional Studies Career Exploration & Development Academic Support Center Course Catalog Office of the Provost Admission Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Tuition & Financial Aid Visit Student Life Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Student Affairs & Campus Life Campus Dining Residential Life Health, Wellness, and Recreation Religious & Spiritual Life Parents and Families About Icon / Caret Created with Sketch. Ithaca College at a Glance Key Facts & Recognition Annual Events Sustainability at Ithaca Strategic Plan Presidential Search Office of the President Icon / Search Icon / Menu Created with Sketch. Icon / Close Created with Sketch. Search Connect With Us Home / Center for Career Exploration and Development / Connect With Us Center for Career Exploration and Development Connect With Us Kamai Career Quest Who We Support First Year Student Second Year Student Third Year Student Fourth Year Student Alumni Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers Inspiring Internships Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging: Our Commitment BIPOC Resources First-Generation Resources International Resources LGBTQIA+ Resources Neurodivergent and Disability Resources Undocumented and DACA Resources Veteran Resources Women Resources Career Toolkit Building Skills Cover Letters Creating A Four Year Plan Exploring Majors Graduate School Interviewing Networking Resumes and CVs Searching For A Job Or Internship Volunteering Abroad Services Online Resources First Destination Survey Student Employment Internship Funding Resources Faculty Toolkit For Employers Gaby Quick Links Annual Report (2024-25) Learn About Career Readiness Recruiting Interest Form Program Request Form NACE 2026 Job Outlook menu Connect with us facebook instagram x Drop-In Hours - No Appointment Needed (Current Students) - Academic Year Only If you've never met with us before, we recommend that you start with a drop-in appointment, which are available from 11:00AM - 2:00 PM, Monday through Friday, no appointment necessary. Drop-in appointments are conducted by our Peer Career Advisors (PCA) , a highly trained team of student staff who can help you with a variety of topics. Not sure what you need? Come see us and we'll help you figure it out. Drop-in hours are not available during the summer.  If you need career support, please schedule an appointment with one of our Career Engagement Specialists. Booking An Appointment With A Professional Staff Member If you've met with a PCA or you are an alumnus , you can also meet with a professional staff member. You can book an appointment with us through the following links: Suzanne Brache : Student Employment Specialist Jonathan Chalmers : School of Business and School of Communications John Fracchia : School of Music, Theatre, & Dance Amy Huang : School of Humanities & Sciences Nico Lanari : School of Health Sciences & Human Performance The CCED Team Suzanne Brache Student Employment Specialist Jonathan Chalmers Career Engagement Specialist, School of Business Nico Lanari Career Engagement Specialist, School of Health Sciences and Human Performance Katrina Clark Associate Director, Experiential Learning and Employer Engagement Dave Curry Director John Fracchia Career Engagement and Technology Specialist, School of Health Sciences and Human Performance Amy Huang Career Engagement Specialist, School of Humanities and Sciences Meet Our Peer Career Advisors (PCAs) - highly trained student employees who are available for drop-ins in the Career Center Monday - Friday from 11am-2pm Angel Angel is a senior majoring in International Business and Advertising, Public Relations & Marketing Communications Colleen Colleen is a senior Advertising, Public Relations, and Marketing Comm major with minors in Graphic Design and Communication. Gaby Gaby is a junior Accounting major with a Business Analytics minor. Jacob Jacob is a junior Documentary Studies and Production major with minors in Marketing, Entrepreneurship & Innovation, and Psych. Jagrit Jagrit is a junior Computer Science major at Ithaca College. Juno Juno Brooks is a fourth year politics major with a history minor. Kamai Kamai is a sophomore Speech-Language Pathology major with an Education Studies minor. Leah Leah is sophomore Occupational Therapy major with a Communication Disorders minor. Nina Nina is a senior Health Sciences Major with a minor in Chemistry. Tamanna Tamanna is a junior Finance major with a minor in Entrepreneurship and Innovation. Ty Ty is a junior Environmental Science and Strategic Leadership double major, with an Entrepreneurship and Innovation minor. Sasha Sasha Culver is a graduate student studying Speech Language Pathology and Audiology. Contact Us Muller Faculty Center 101 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 Office Hours: M-F from 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM Drop-In Hours: M-F from 11:00 AM - 2:00 PM Meet Our Staff careers@ithaca.edu 607-274-3365 Connect with us facebook instagram x 953 Danby Road, Ithaca, NY 14850 (607) 274-3011 Footer Campus Store Accessibility Guide Safety and Emergency Visit Make a Gift Campus Map Contact Directory Employment Campus Services facebook icon Created with Sketch. Facebook instagram icon Created with Sketch. Instagram youtube icon Created with Sketch. YouTube Threads icon Threads TikTock icon TikTok © 2026 Ithaca College. All rights reserved Non-Discrimination Statement | Privacy Policy"
    }
